# 2️⃣0️⃣ Priority Queue

A Priority Queue is a data structure where elements are processed according to their priority.

A Heap is commonly used to implement a Priority Queue.

Example:

```text
Normal Queue:

First In → First Out
```

Priority Queue:

```text
Highest / Lowest Priority → First
```

---

# 2️⃣1️⃣ C++ Priority Queue

By default, C++ provides a **Max Heap**.

```cpp
priority_queue<int> pq;
```

Example:

```cpp
pq.push(10);
pq.push(30);
pq.push(20);

cout << pq.top();
```

Output:

```text
30
```

Because the largest element has the highest priority.

---

# 2️⃣2️⃣ Min Heap Using Priority Queue

Use:

```cpp
priority_queue<
    int,
    vector<int>,
    greater<int>
> pq;
```

Example:

```cpp
priority_queue<
    int,
    vector<int>,
    greater<int>
> pq;

pq.push(10);
pq.push(30);
pq.push(20);

cout << pq.top();
```

Output:

```text
10
```

