# 📊 Heap Complexity

| Operation | Complexity |
|-----------|------------|
| Get Min/Max | O(1) |
| Insert | O(log n) |
| Delete Root | O(log n) |
| Heapify | O(log n) |
| Build Heap | O(n) |
| Search | O(n) |

---

# 2️⃣4️⃣ Why is Heap Search O(n)?

Unlike a BST, a Heap is **not globally sorted**.

Example:

```text
        5
       / \
      10  7
     / \
    20 15
```

Searching for:

```text
15
```

cannot simply decide:

```text
Go Left
or
Go Right
```

Therefore, searching may require checking many nodes.

```text
Search → O(n)
```

---

# 2️⃣5️⃣ Heap vs BST

| Feature | Heap | BST |
|---------|------|-----|
| Root | Min/Max | Depends on tree |
| Global Ordering | No | Yes |
| Search | O(n) | O(log n) average |
| Min/Max | O(1) | O(h) |
| Insert | O(log n) | O(h) |
| Delete Root | O(log n) | Depends |
| Common Use | Priority Queue | Searching |

